WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.334
-How great is it
to hear an audience?

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:04.801
-Oh, my God, it's amazing.
It feels new.

00:00:04.801 --> 00:00:06.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Right. It's amazing.

00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:07.567
-Thank you.
Thank you.

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:10.400
-Thank you for coming in studio
and for doing this.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.167
-I mean, yeah,
I'm so excited to be back

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:15.167
out in the world a little bit.
-Yeah, right?

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:18.067
You know, I'm a fan of yours,
but I loved your movie --

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:19.601
I love your stand-up,
but I love your movie,

00:00:19.601 --> 00:00:21.434
"The Big Sick."
It's one of my favorites.

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:24.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
Phenomenal job.

00:00:24.033 --> 00:00:26.133
But now you are a superhero.

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:28.434
You're --
You're a superhero, dude.

00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:30.868
-I can't believe it.
I really can't.

00:00:30.868 --> 00:00:33.200
I'll know Friday,
when the movie comes out,

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.133
that it's not
an elaborate prank.

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:36.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:37.601
-No, it's not a prank.
You're real.

00:00:37.601 --> 00:00:40.167
-It feels wild, man.
-How did it come about?

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:42.868
Did you get the call from --
Who called you?

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:45.667
-So, I'm out of town
for a few weeks,

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:49.067
and I get a call, and they say,
"Hey, Marvel wants to meet you."

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:50.467
And I was like,
"What does that mean?

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:53.234
Marvel's not a person, like --"
-No, no, exactly right.

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:56.167
-"What do you mean?"
They're like, "Chloé Zhao

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:58.400
and Nate Moore, a producer,
want to meet you."

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:02.000
And I knew Chloé
was directing "Eternals."

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.300
Amazing director,
huge fan of hers.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.834
I don't know why
they want to meet me.

00:01:05.834 --> 00:01:08.501
-Yeah.
-So I have this meeting.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:11.567
And Chloé talks me through
the entire movie in 45 minutes.

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:13.434
She's like, 45 minutes,
beginning to end,

00:01:13.434 --> 00:01:15.067
tells me the entire movie.

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:17.567
And then she's like,
"So, what do you think?"

00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:19.901
And I was like, "What do you --
It sounds great.

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:21.801
I'd love to go watch it."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.801 --> 00:01:23.667
"Are you just, like..."
-"Sounds like a hit, yeah."

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:24.934
I mean --
-"Yeah, do that.

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:27.367
That sounds great."
-"What do you want me for?"

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:29.267
-"You're gonna make millions."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.267 --> 00:01:30.667
"You just wanted my feedback?

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:32.434
It is a thumbs-up from me,
Chloé."

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:34.367
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:35.501
-I was like, "Thumbs up."
And she's like,

00:01:35.501 --> 00:01:37.667
"No.
Do you want to be in it?"

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:40.901
And I said yes before she had
finished the sentence.

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:42.434
[ Laughter ]
Which you should not do,

00:01:42.434 --> 00:01:44.300
'cause what you do is,
"Let me think about it,"

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:46.334
then you go tell your agent
to try and get you more money.

00:01:46.334 --> 00:01:48.868
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
-I was like, "Yes! Of course!

00:01:48.868 --> 00:01:50.133
I'll pay you to do it,
whatever."

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:51.868
[ Laughter ]
-Exactly correct.

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:53.734
-"Whatever needs done."
-You pay them to --

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:55.133
I'll pay you to be
in a Marvel movie.

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:57.501
You have your own
action figure, buddy.

00:01:57.501 --> 00:02:01.567
Look at this.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:05.834
-Look at him!
[ Laughing ]

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:07.934
-I mean, how cool is that?

00:02:07.934 --> 00:02:10.334
In your wildest dreams,
did you ever go, like,

00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:12.567
"Oh, yeah,
I'm gonna be a superhero,

00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:13.934
and I'm gonna have a doll,

00:02:13.934 --> 00:02:16.200
and kids are gonna buy my doll
in the toy store."

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.133
-It's not a doll,
it's an action figure.

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:20.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:23.367
You know, the difference
is points of articulation.

00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:26.133
I say that because I own
a lot of action figures.

00:02:26.133 --> 00:02:28.033
-Oh, you do?
-Yeah, I buy them.

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:32.033
And, yeah, it's really,
really unbelievable.

00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:37.300
You know, when I first saw it,
I was just so happy,

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:40.033
and then I was like, "Emily,
they messed up my profile."

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:41.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:42.801
And she was like,
"No, they didn't."

00:02:42.801 --> 00:02:44.467
-They nailed it, yeah.
-She was like,

00:02:44.467 --> 00:02:46.734
"They got it exactly right."
-Yeah.

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:49.000
-Because I was like,
"Stuff is sticking out

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.133
where it shouldn't
be sticking out

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:51.801
and not sticking out
where it should be,"

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:53.367
and she was like, "Well,
that's how your face looks."

00:02:53.367 --> 00:02:54.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:58.033
-Tell everybody about your
character and your superpower.

00:02:58.033 --> 00:03:01.667
-So I play a character
named Kingo, and, you know,

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:04.467
Eternals have sort of been
on Earth for 7,000 years,

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:07.067
we're here to fight
these monsters called Deviants,

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:09.267
and we're sort of
all supposed to go off

00:03:09.267 --> 00:03:10.934
on our own
and keep a low profile.

00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:12.434
-Yeah.
-And so my character

00:03:12.434 --> 00:03:14.767
goes and becomes
a Bollywood movie star.

00:03:14.767 --> 00:03:16.234
[ Cheers ]
That's sort of --

00:03:16.234 --> 00:03:19.167
-Kind of the opposite, yeah.
-Yeah. Yeah, he does.

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:21.133
But he's just --
You know, so many superheroes,

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:24.234
like, the power is, like,
a big responsibility on them.

00:03:24.234 --> 00:03:25.968
You know, this guy loves it.

00:03:25.968 --> 00:03:28.467
He loves being a superhero.
He loves having powers.

00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:30.000
He loves being
a Bollywood movie star.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.234
No notes, his life is perfect.
-Yeah.

00:03:32.234 --> 00:03:34.801
You do a big, giant
Bollywood dance number.

00:03:34.801 --> 00:03:37.100
-Yeah, and we're gonna show
a clip from that a little bit,

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.100
you know, so...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:41.367
-I didn't know --
Do you know how to do this?

00:03:41.367 --> 00:03:43.801
-Well, no,
I don't know how to do this.

00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:46.067
Emily can't even get me
on the dance floor to dance,

00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:48.701
and I was like, "In front of
millions of people?

00:03:48.701 --> 00:03:50.968
I can't do this."
So when I first met Chloé,

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:52.734
she was like, "You're gonna do
a Bollywood dance number,"

00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:55.767
and I was like,
"Can we do something else?"

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:57.400
-Yeah, anything else, yeah.
-And she was like,

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.033
"Okay. We'll do
a Bollywood action sequence."

00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:00.834
I was like, "Great."
And then, we got to London

00:04:00.834 --> 00:04:02.534
to shoot it, she was like,
"I lied.

00:04:02.534 --> 00:04:04.434
It's a Bollywood dance number."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:07.200
She lied to me.
She put a lie in the script.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.267 --> 00:04:10.567
She printed out the lie.
-Yeah.

00:04:10.567 --> 00:04:13.868
-And so I got a --
I was like, "Get me a teacher,"

00:04:13.868 --> 00:04:15.767
and we -- I trained for
four months to do it.

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:16.968
But it was really cool,
you know?

00:04:16.968 --> 00:04:18.634
The first --
So, I trained with --

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:19.701
Milika is her name.

00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:22.033
She choreographed
the dance, too.

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:24.767
And when I first walked in
to the big rehearsal

00:04:24.767 --> 00:04:26.767
with everybody,
I walked into the gym

00:04:26.767 --> 00:04:28.467
where we were doing
the rehearsal.

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:29.601
And I got really emotional.

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:31.767
It was like 50
South Asian people.

00:04:31.767 --> 00:04:33.667
[ Cheers ]
And I was like --

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:35.200
Yeah, man!
Cheer for South Asia!

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:37.901 --> 00:04:40.601
So many years, you barely have
any South Asian people,

00:04:40.601 --> 00:04:42.934
and then suddenly,
there's like 52 of us

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:44.868
in one scene, you know?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:46.467
It was awesome!
-Yeah.

00:04:46.467 --> 00:04:49.334
-And it's, you know, it's
a little tough 'cause it's --

00:04:49.334 --> 00:04:53.234
There are 52 people, and 51 of
them are professional dancers.

00:04:53.234 --> 00:04:55.701
[ Laughter ]
And the one who's in focus

00:04:55.701 --> 00:04:58.200
is really trying to hang on.
-Oh, no, no, no.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:00.200
I got to say, I'm just --

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.767
I'm happy for you.
Couldn't happen to nicer guy.

00:05:02.767 --> 00:05:04.000
-Oh, thank you.
-All the success.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:07.067
But this is major
on so many levels.

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:08.267
-I love this movie so much.

00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:09.701
I'm just so thrilled
to be a part of it.

00:05:09.701 --> 00:05:11.467
-Good man.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:11.467 --> 00:05:12.868
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:12.868 --> 00:05:15.167
Here's Kumail Nanjiani
in "Eternals."

00:05:15.167 --> 00:05:16.434
Take a look.

00:05:16.434 --> 00:05:21.901
♪♪

00:05:21.901 --> 00:05:23.467
[ Music stops ]

00:05:23.467 --> 00:05:25.667
-Cut!
Okay, everyone.

00:05:25.667 --> 00:05:26.934
That was good.

00:05:26.934 --> 00:05:29.734
Think we can do 10% better.
That was beautiful.

00:05:29.734 --> 00:05:31.801
Very, very good.

00:05:31.801 --> 00:05:33.234
Aah!

00:05:33.234 --> 00:05:36.300
All my friends from college
are here.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:38.968
Boss!
Perfect timing.

00:05:38.968 --> 00:05:43.300
Welcome to the set of...
[ Speaking Hindi ]

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:45.067
I'm playing you!
You like the costume?

00:05:45.067 --> 00:05:46.267
-We need to talk.

00:05:46.267 --> 00:05:47.667
-Tell the director
I have some notes for him.

00:05:47.667 --> 00:05:49.501
-We need to talk to you
in private.

00:05:49.501 --> 00:05:51.534
-Oh, Karun? He's worked
with me for 50 years.

00:05:51.534 --> 00:05:53.167
I trust him completely.

00:05:53.167 --> 00:05:55.601
Actually, when we first met,
he thought I was vampire,

00:05:55.601 --> 00:05:57.434
and he tried
to stake me through the heart.

00:05:57.434 --> 00:05:59.567
-I have apologized
so many times.

00:05:59.567 --> 00:06:01.434
-Not quite enough times.
Very close, though.

00:06:01.434 --> 00:06:02.634
I'll let you know.

00:06:02.634 --> 00:06:03.701
-That's what I'm talking about,
come on.

00:06:03.701 --> 00:06:05.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
Very funny, bud.

00:06:05.734 --> 00:06:07.334
Kumail Nanjiani, everybody!

00:06:07.334 --> 00:06:10.968
"Eternals" opens in theaters
this Friday.

